/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Fatigue is failure under a stress that repeats.
   - Stage 1, crack initiation.
   - Stage 2, crack growth.
   - Stage 3, final fracture.
   - The R.
   - Plotted on log–log axes, steel results lie close to a straight line from about (10³, 0.9Sut) to (10⁶, Se), where Se is the endurance limit.
   - b = (1/3) log₁₀(Se/0.9Sut) log₁₀ Sf = log₁₀(0.9Sut) + b(log₁₀ N − 3)
   - Sf is the fatigue strength (the amplitude that gives a life of N cycles) in MPa; b is the slope per decade of N.
   - Ferrous metals show a knee at about 10⁶ cycles (some books use 10⁷); below Se they survive indefinitely.
   - Se′ is the endurance limit of the small polished test bar.
*/
