/* book Worked example 2: Q: A solid round bar is used as a beam that does not rotate. At its critical section the bending moment varies from 100 N·m to 400 N·m. The steel has Syt = 400 MPa and Se = 230 MPa (corrected), Kf = 1.5 at the section, and n = 2. Find the diameter by the Soderberg line.
   1. Mean and alternating moments: Mm = (400 + 100)/2 = 250 N·m = 250 000 N·mm; Ma = (400 − 100)/2 = 150 N·m = 150 000 N·mm.
   2. Stresses: σm = 32Mm/(πd³) and σa = 32Ma/(πd³), with Kf on σa.
   3. Soderberg: 1/n = Kf σa/Se + σm/Syt = (32/(πd³)) × (1.5 × 150 000/230 + 250 000/400).
   4. Bracket: 978.3 + 625.0 = 1603.3 N·mm per MPa.
   5. d³ = 2 × 32 × 1603.3/π = 32 661 mm³, so d = 31.97 mm. Choose d = 32 mm.
   6. Check at 32 mm: σm = 77.71 MPa, σa = 46.63 MPa, Kf σa = 69.94 MPa; 1/n = 69.94/230 + 77.71/400 = 0.3041 + 0.1943 = 0.4984, so n = 2.01.
   Answer: d = 31.97 mm, rounded to 32 mm, which gives n = 2.01 by Soderberg. */
